From e2365ec884f6f5dd5f686b1d256a46f39ed0b84f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:52:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jm-v7 010: Bifrost robustBufferAccess2 and nullDescriptor

VK_EXT_robustness2 on v6/v7, ported from JimVulkan/mesa-unified-drivers
(MIT, Copyright 2026 XclipseTools). The v9/v10 work (jm-v9 010/030,
csf-v11 122/181/184) is Valhall-only (LEA_BUF texel checks, Valhall
NULL_DESCRIPTOR, LD_TEX alpha fix-up) and does not apply here.

- Bifrost has no NULL descriptor. The device keeps a zeroed 4 KiB BO and,
  built through its own entry points, a 1x1 image view with a ZERO
  swizzle. A null write copies: that view's texture descriptor (sampled
  images, combined image samplers, input attachments), its storage image
  attribute buffer with size 0 (storage images), a 0-element texel buffer
  on the zero BO (texel buffers), a size-0 SSBO on the zero BO, or a
  256-entry UBO on the zero BO (UBOs and dynamic UBOs: JimVulkan measured
  a 0-entry UBO end the job TERMINATED and pointer 0 read-fault).
- Null vertex buffers point at the zero BO instead of address 0.
- Null SSBOs need the bounds-checked address format, so null descriptors
  turn SSBO robustness on (panvk_ssbo_robustness()).
- The Bifrost null-descriptor asserts in the size/levels/samples queries
  are gone: a query through a null image reports the 1x1 image.
- robustBufferAccess2 relies on the bounded SSBO format (software) and on
  the hardware bounds of UBO, attribute and texel buffer descriptors, as
  JimVulkan reports for G52/G72/G76. robustImageAccess2 stays off on
  v6/v7.

Build-tested only, no Bifrost device run. biblioklept

